# F-02 planner-owned acceptance baseline — REVISION 4 (read-only)
#
# Prepared 2026-10-05 by the planner/test-owner session, after the independent
# correction-implementation re-review (docs/reviews/F-02-correction-implementation.md,
# CHANGES_REQUIRED) found C1: a successful restoration response whose JSON body
# cannot be decoded rejects the client helper without cleanup, leaving the stored
# token and emitting an unhandled rejection.
#
# REVISION HISTORY
#   rev 1-2 (2026-10-03) superseded; rev 2 archived at F-02-tests-rev2.sha256.
#   rev 3   (2026-10-04) the approved correction-batch checkpoint. ARCHIVED
#                   byte-for-byte at docs/handoffs/F-02-tests-rev3.sha256; the
#                   archive's own SHA-256 is
#                   9c46ed067212f826e9721a87bdc1d7ab3959ed33ea31db9572383b1f49ac79fc,
#                   exactly the value recorded as the approved checkpoint in
#                   docs/reviews/F-02-preparation-revision-3-followup.md.
#                   Do not regenerate the archive. Running sha256sum -c on it now
#                   yields 22 OK / 2 FAILED: the two failures are precisely the
#                   client acceptance files this revision extends for C1.
#   rev 4   (2026-10-05) 24 entries, same paths, 2 refreshes. Changes only:
#                   - Both client auth suites gain a C1 regression block:
#                     * a stored token plus a successful /auth/session response
#                       whose json() rejects must be treated as no session, with
#                       no unhandled rejection, the token removed, the login
#                       screen visible and protected content absent;
#                     * a valid-restoration control and a decoded-invalid-schema
#                       control are retained;
#                     * a stale decoding/read failure released after a newer
#                       successful login must not erase that login.
#                   The stub helper gains an additive `sessionJsonThrows` option;
#                   every pre-existing assertion is preserved.
#                   No production change is authorised by this manifest.
#
# Earlier baselines remain unchanged and must continue to verify:
#   docs/handoffs/S-01-tests.sha256            11 entries
#   docs/handoffs/F-01-tests.sha256            14 entries
#   docs/handoffs/F-01-corrections-tests.sha256 10 entries
# docs/reviews/F-01-accepted.sha256 still reports 28/33, with exactly the five
# documented F-02 extensions diverging and no F-01 source regression.
#
# Do not regenerate this manifest to fix a failure. Any further revision is a
# numbered rev with its own recorded reason.
